§§ `Offences and punishment (Part XX)`

-- Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document?
-- s 250(1), (3), (4): an untrue statement or an omission of a material fact in a document the Act requires to be sent; not the register of individuals with significant control; no offence for one who neither knew nor could with reasonable diligence have known.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for a false or misleading report, return, notice or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- What is the largest fine I could face for a false or misleading document?
-- s 250(1): a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I could face for a false or misleading document` EQUALS 5000
-- What is the longest imprisonment I could face for a false or misleading document?
-- s 250(1): imprisonment not exceeding six months.
#ASSERT `What is the longest imprisonment I could face for a false or misleading document` EQUALS 6
-- As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document?
-- s 250(2), (3): a director or officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced is a party to the offence, unless the s 250(3) immunity applies.
#ASSERT `As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`As a director or officer, am I guilty when my body corporate files a false or misleading document` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- What is the largest fine I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document?
-- s 250(2) with s 250(1): the same punishment, a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document` EQUALS 5000
-- What is the longest imprisonment I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document?
-- s 250(2) with s 250(1): imprisonment not exceeding six months.
#ASSERT `What is the longest imprisonment I could face as a director or officer who authorized the false or misleading document` EQUALS 6
-- Am I guilty of an offence for contravening a provision that has no stated punishment (s 251)?
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening a provision that has no stated punishment` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for contravening a provision that has no stated punishment` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I guilty of an offence for contravening a provision that has no stated punishment` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Does the Act itself state a maximum punishment for the general offence?
-- s 251: an offence punishable on summary conviction, with no maximum stated in the section.
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act itself state a maximum punishment for the general offence`
-- Can the court order me to comply with the Act after I am convicted (s 252(1))?
#ASSERT `Can the court order me to comply with the Act after I am convicted` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the court order me to comply with the Act after I am convicted` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the court order me to comply with the Act after I am convicted` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- By what day can a prosecution be brought against me for an offence under the Act (s 252(2))?
#ASSERT `By what day can a prosecution be brought against me for an offence under the Act` (YMD 2024 6 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 15
#ASSERT `By what day can a prosecution be brought against me for an offence under the Act` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
-- Is it too late to prosecute me for an offence under the Act?
-- s 252(2): two years after the subject-matter arose; the anniversary itself is in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it too late to prosecute me for an offence under the Act` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`Is it too late to prosecute me for an offence under the Act` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2024 6 15))
#ASSERT `Is it too late to prosecute me for an offence under the Act` (YMD 2024 6 15) (YMD 2026 6 16)
-- Is my civil remedy suspended or affected because the same act is an offence under the Act?
-- s 252(3): a civil remedy is not suspended or affected by reason only that the act or omission is an offence under the Act.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my civil remedy suspended or affected because the same act is an offence under the Act`

